; Collection over abort, across a syntax error. A stray close delimiter sits
; between two forms that each violate the schema the same way. Both
; violations must be reported: a host that stopped validating at the first
; syntax error would emit only the first, and a host that discarded the
; whole tree would emit neither.
;
; A stray `)` is used rather than an unclosed form or an unterminated string
; because those two swallow the rest of the file into the recovered node —
; the tail would then be validated *nested*, which pins recovery shape
; instead of the continuation this case is about.
;
; Ordering is part of the contract: `Host.validateDocument` runs parse as
; its own phase, so the syntax diagnostic precedes both validation
; diagnostics even though its source position sits between them.
(plugin :name p :version "1.0.0"
  (form :name pt (key :name x :type number)))

(pt :x "before")
)
(pt :x "after")
